<td id="S3.T1.9.22.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">0.41</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Maximal aggregation.</span>
For each <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we aggregate the maximal PMI over text tokens <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and over selected vision tokens <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the crossmodal and internal relevance scores:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{i}^{\mathrm{cross}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cross</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{i}^{\mathrm{cross}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{T}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{T}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{i}^{\mathrm{self}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>self</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{i}^{\mathrm{self}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{S}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{S}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">The max aggregation forces <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{\mathrm{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{\mathrm{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> to capture the strongest crossmodal relevance (”pivot word”) and intra-modal redundancy (”pivot patch”), leading to consistently better performance than the global average.
See justification in App. <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Maximal Aggregation ‣ Appendix A Theory ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Global aggregation.</span>
Another way is to the full MI formulation, <span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, averaging over all text tokens or selected image tokens (”consensus”), interpreted as global aggregation:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{i}^{\mathrm{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{i}^{\mathrm{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{X}}\underbrace{p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{j})}_{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})}\cdot{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{j})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{X}}\underbrace{p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{j})}_{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})}\cdot{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{j})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Empirical comparisons of the two aggregation strategies are presented in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Greedy search.</span>
For greedy search, we define a scoring function <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as the marginal gain of adding <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> balances the relevance and redundancy:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{i}=\lambda S_{i}^{\mathrm{cross}}-(1-\lambda)\cdot S_{i}^{\mathrm{self}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cross</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>self</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{i}=\lambda S_{i}^{\mathrm{cross}}-(1-\lambda)\cdot S_{i}^{\mathrm{self}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda\cdot\underbrace{\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{T}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})}}_{\text{relevance}\rightarrow\text{sorting}}-(1-\lambda)\underbrace{\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{v}_{j}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{S}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})}}_{\text{redundancy}\rightarrow\text{greedy}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>relevance</mtext><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>sorting</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>redundancy</mtext><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>greedy</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda\cdot\underbrace{\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{T}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})}}_{\text{relevance}\rightarrow\text{sorting}}-(1-\lambda)\underbrace{\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{v}_{j}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{S}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})}}_{\text{redundancy}\rightarrow\text{greedy}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math> considers only crossmodal relevance towards user prompts, and <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> measures only internal redundancy.
According to the budget <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{keep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{keep}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conduct a greedy search to find <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes the marginal gain at each step:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{v}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{v}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\arg\max_{\mathbf{v}_{i}\in\mathcal{V}\setminus\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}}S_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\arg\max_{\mathbf{v}_{i}\in\mathcal{V}\setminus\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}}S_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">MI-Pruner</span></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span>
Visual and textual embeddings <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\{\mathbf{v}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N_{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\{\mathbf{v}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N_{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}=\{\mathbf{t}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}=\{\mathbf{t}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
temperature <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>,
budget <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{keep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{keep}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span>
The selected visual subset <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// Similarity matrices</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}\leftarrow\mathbf{v}_{i}/\lVert\mathbf{v}_{i}\rVert,\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\leftarrow\mathbf{t}_{j}/\lVert\mathbf{t}_{j}\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}\leftarrow\mathbf{v}_{i}/\lVert\mathbf{v}_{i}\rVert,\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\leftarrow\mathbf{t}_{j}/\lVert\mathbf{t}_{j}\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\rho}^{\mathrm{cross}}_{ij}\leftarrow\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}/\tau,\bm{\rho}^{\mathrm{self}}_{ij}\leftarrow\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>cross</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>self</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\rho}^{\mathrm{cross}}_{ij}\leftarrow\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}/\tau,\bm{\rho}^{\mathrm{self}}_{ij}\leftarrow\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}/\tau</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// Derive distributions</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
             
<div id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:341.6pt;height:16.6pt;vertical-align:-4.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(53.5pt,-2.6pt) scale(1.4558423851627,1.4558423851627) ;">
<p id="alg1.l7.3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}|\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})\leftarrow\text{softmax}_{j}(\bm{\rho}^{\mathrm{cross}}_{ij}),\ p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}|\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})\leftarrow\text{softmax}_{j}(\bm{\rho}^{\mathrm{self}}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>cross</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>self</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}|\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})\leftarrow\text{softmax}_{j}(\bm{\rho}^{\mathrm{cross}}_{ij}),\ p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}|\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})\leftarrow\text{softmax}_{j}(\bm{\rho}^{\mathrm{self}}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})\leftarrow\frac{1}{N_{V}},p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})\leftarrow\frac{1}{N_{V}}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{V}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})\leftarrow\frac{1}{N_{V}},p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})\leftarrow\frac{1}{N_{V}}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{V}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// Pointwise Mutual Information (PMI)</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
             
<div id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:341.6pt;height:13.8pt;vertical-align:-3.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(42.3pt,-1.7pt) scale(1.32888642499168,1.32888642499168) ;">
<p id="alg1.l10.3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})\leftarrow\log\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})}{p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})},\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})\leftarrow\log\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})}{p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})\leftarrow\log\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})}{p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})},\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})\leftarrow\log\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})}{p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// Greedy selection</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}|&lt;N_{\mathrm{keep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}|&lt;N_{\mathrm{keep}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}\in\mathcal{V}\setminus\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}\in\mathcal{V}\setminus\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{\mathrm{cross}}\leftarrow\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{T}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cross</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{\mathrm{cross}}\leftarrow\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{T}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{\mathrm{self}}\leftarrow\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{S}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>self</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{\mathrm{self}}\leftarrow\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j}\in\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{S}}}{\mathrm{PMI}(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i};\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}\leftarrow\lambda S_{i}^{\mathrm{cross}}-(1-\lambda)S_{i}^{\mathrm{self}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cross</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>self</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}\leftarrow\lambda S_{i}^{\mathrm{cross}}-(1-\lambda)S_{i}^{\mathrm{self}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}^{\star}\leftarrow\arg\max_{\mathbf{v}_{i}}S_{i},\text{and}~\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\leftarrow\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\cup\{\mathbf{v}^{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}^{\star}\leftarrow\arg\max_{\mathbf{v}_{i}}S_{i},\text{and}~\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\leftarrow\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\cup\{\mathbf{v}^{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}\leftarrow\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}\leftarrow\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Efficient Inference</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall Sec. <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 MLLM Architecture ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">MI-Pruner</span> prunes vision tokens to a smaller set <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the projection space, Eqn. (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 2.1 MLLM Architecture ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) is updated to:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}\oplus\mathcal{T}\in\mathbb{R}^{(N_{\mathrm{keep}}+N_{T})\times d},~N_{\mathrm{keep}}&lt;N_{V}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{keep}}\oplus\mathcal{T}\in\mathbb{R}^{(N_{\mathrm{keep}}+N_{T})\times d},~N_{\mathrm{keep}}&lt;N_{V}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <span id="S3.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">MI-Pruner</span> doesn’t require attention collection or interaction of LLM, the scoring calculation is very efficient with minimal latency, and the subset selection problem becomes <em id="S3.SS3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">modular</em> instead of just submodular.
Our selection has a complexity of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N_{V}+N_{\mathrm{keep}}\log N_{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N_{V}+N_{\mathrm{keep}}\log N_{V})</annotation></semantics></math>,<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            The computation requires <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N_{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N_{V})</annotation></semantics></math> evaluations of the <math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{PMI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PMI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{PMI}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="footnote2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N_{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N_{V})</annotation></semantics></math> cost for building a heap, and <math id="footnote2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{keep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{keep}}</annotation></semantics></math> retrievals of the largest element in the heap, each of which costs <math id="footnote2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\log N_{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\log N_{V})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span> while the classic greedy search holds <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N_{V}N_{\mathrm{keep}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N_{V}N_{\mathrm{keep}})</annotation></semantics></math>. We expect that in settings of interest <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{keep}}\log N_{V}&lt;N_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>keep</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{keep}}\log N_{V}&lt;N_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, implying an overall complexity of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N_{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N_{V})</annotation></semantics></math>.
See Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 MI-Pruner ‣ 3 Methods ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for our full pipeline. Then, we empirically verify that this faster inference framework results in comparable or better performance to SOTA baselines.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experiments Setup</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Settings.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for open-ended QA datasets, involving GQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hudson and Manning, 2019</a>)</cite> and MMVet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math> for broader closed-form-type datasets, including SQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2022</a>)</cite> (mutiple-choice), TextVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Singh et al., 2019</a>)</cite> (reference answer provided), MME<sub id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">P</sub> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> (Yes/No) and POPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025</a>)</cite> (Yes/No).
The inference and evaluation follow the default settings and metrics. Specifically, we conduct bootstrapping for MMVet since it includes only 218 samples,
and report F1 score (P<sub id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub">F1</sub>) and Yes-rate (P<sub id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sub">Yes</sub>) for POPE as fine-grained measures.
The MLLMs include LLaVA1.5-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>, Qwen2VL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and latest Qwen3VL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, all in greedy sampling and SDPA attention, more details in App. <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Large-scale Models and Diverse Settings ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>. For generalization, we also apply our method to Video-LLaVA-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2024</a>)</cite> with <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> and test on TGIF-QA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jang et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, MSVD-QA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2017</a>)</cite> and MSRVTT-QA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2017</a>)</cite> datasets.
All experiments are conducted on a single NVIDIA A100 GPU.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
