<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:173%;">Appendix<span id="p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theory</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Definition</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Shannon Entropy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kraskov et al., 2004</a>; <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray, 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gallager, 1968</a>)</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Shannon entropy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(X)</annotation></semantics></math> of a random variable <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> measures the average uncertainty or information content associated with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(X)=-\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}p(x)\log p(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(X)=-\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}p(x)\log p(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional Entropy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kraskov et al., 2004</a>; <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray, 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gallager, 1968</a>)</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two random variables <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional entropy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(X|Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(X|Y)</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the amount of information needed to describe <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> given that known <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(X|Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(X|Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{u\in\mathcal{X},y\in\mathcal{Y}}p(x,y)\log p(x|y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{u\in\mathcal{X},y\in\mathcal{Y}}p(x,y)\log p(x|y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional Mutual Information <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gallager, 1968</a>)</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Conditional Mutual Information <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MI}(X;Y\mid Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MI}(X;Y\mid Z)</annotation></semantics></math> measures the reduction in uncertainty of a random variable <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> when additionally knowing <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MI}(X;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MI}(X;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y\mid Z)=H(X\mid Z)-H(X\mid Y,Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y\mid Z)=H(X\mid Z)-H(X\mid Y,Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X},\,y\in\mathcal{Y},\,z\in\mathcal{Z}}p(x,y,z)\log\frac{p(x\mid y,z)}{p(x\mid z)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X},\,y\in\mathcal{Y},\,z\in\mathcal{Z}}p(x,y,z)\log\frac{p(x\mid y,z)}{p(x\mid z)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Submodular Function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fujishige, 2005</a>)</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set. A set function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:2^{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:2^{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is called submodular if for every <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\subseteq X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(A\cup B)+f(A\cap B)\leq f(A)+f(B)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(A\cup B)+f(A\cap B)\leq f(A)+f(B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An equivalent and often more intuitive definition is based on the <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">marginal gain</span>, as shown in the main paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Conditional Independence</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="104.55" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 104.55" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,104.55) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#0000B3;" fill="#0000B3" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.98 L 0 95.57 C 0 100.53 4.02 104.55 8.98 104.55 L 468.4 104.55 C 473.36 104.55 477.38 100.53 477.38 95.57 L 477.38 8.98 C 477.38 4.02 473.36 0 468.4 0 L 8.98 0 C 4.02 0 0 4.02 0 8.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7F7FF;" fill="#F7F7FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 8.98 L 1.11 95.57 C 1.11 99.92 4.63 103.45 8.98 103.45 L 468.4 103.45 C 472.74 103.45 476.27 99.92 476.27 95.57 L 476.27 8.98 C 476.27 4.63 472.74 1.11 468.4 1.11 L 8.98 1.11 C 4.63 1.11 1.11 4.63 1.11 8.98 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.79 32.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.5em;--ltx-fo-height:4.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.39em;font-size:10pt;" height="78.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 59.42)" width="435.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.5em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Assumption:<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The candidate <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐯</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the selected set <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This assumption helps to maintain submodularity and derive tractable marginal gains.<span id="A1.SS2.p1.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Mutual Information is widely recognized for exhibiting submodularity (the property of diminishing returns) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Iyer et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Krause et al., 2008</a>)</cite>, providing a principled foundation for efficient subset selection.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To rigorously adapt MI-based submodular optimization to the token selection task, we bring the Naive Bayes assumption as the conditional independence between <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. From the view of probability and mutual information, it holds:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\mathbf{v}_{i},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\mathbf{v}_{i},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p(\mathbf{v}_{i}\mid\mathcal{T})p(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p(\mathbf{v}_{i}\mid\mathcal{T})p(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This assumption has two immediate consequences:
(i) <span id="A1.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">submodular</span> guarantees for the property of diminishing returns; (ii) a tractable derivation of the <span id="A1.SS2.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">marginal gain</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Submodularity.</span> The conditional independence assumes that a single patch is sufficiently representative of a semantic unit.
A counterexample is that, if a semantic concept strictly requires the joint presence of multiple patches (e.g., both a left and a right part), then adding the remaining patch at a later stage could violate the diminishing-returns property. Nevertheless, the assumption of semantic sufficiency is well justified in practice. For example, a single patch depicting a “wheel” or a “grille” is often sufficient to convey the semantic concept of “<span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">_car</span>”.
Based on this assumption, we can robustly treat the visual token selection process as a submodular maximization problem, ensuring both theoretical consistency and computational efficiency.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Marginal gains.</span> Since accurately estimating the joint distribution involving <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is high-dimensional infeasible, we approximate the conditional mutual information by the marginal mutual information.
According to Def. <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 2.1 (Mutual Information ( , )). ‣ 2.3 Information Theory ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>,
Mutual information can be expressed in terms of entropy:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MI}(X;Y)=H(Y)-H(Y\mid X)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MI}(X;Y)=H(Y)-H(Y\mid X).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Here, we give the proof from Eqn. (<a href="#S2.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 2.3 Information Theory ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) to Eqn. (<a href="#S2.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 2.3 Information Theory ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MI}(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\cup\{\mathbf{v}_{i}\};\mathcal{T})-\mathrm{MI}(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}};\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MI}(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\cup\{\mathbf{v}_{i}\};\mathcal{T})-\mathrm{MI}(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}};\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\cancel{H(\mathcal{T})}-H(\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\cup\{\mathbf{v}_{i}\})\right]-\left[\cancel{H(\mathcal{T})}-H(\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><menclose notation="updiagonalstrike"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><menclose notation="updiagonalstrike"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\cancel{H(\mathcal{T})}-H(\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\cup\{\mathbf{v}_{i}\})\right]-\left[\cancel{H(\mathcal{T})}-H(\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})-H(\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\cup\{\mathbf{v}_{i}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})-H(\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\cup\{\mathbf{v}_{i}\})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Further, this conditional MI can be written as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})=\underbrace{\operatorname{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})}_{\operatorname{MI}^{\mathrm{cross}}}-\underbrace{\operatorname{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})}_{\operatorname{MI}^{\mathrm{self}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>MI</mi><mi>cross</mi></msup></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>MI</mi><mi>self</mi></msup></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})=\underbrace{\operatorname{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})}_{\operatorname{MI}^{\mathrm{cross}}}-\underbrace{\operatorname{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})}_{\operatorname{MI}^{\mathrm{self}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})+\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T})-\operatorname{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})+\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T})-\operatorname{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">However, the crossmodal term is intractable, which causes trouble in deriving the marginal gain <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, we leverage the conditional independence assumption, and substitute Eqn. (<a href="#A1.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ A.2 Conditional Independence ‣ Appendix A Theory ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) into Eqn. (<a href="#A1.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ A.2 Conditional Independence ‣ Appendix A Theory ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>). Since <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cancel{\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="updiagonalstrike"><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cancel{\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain an estimator:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mathrm{MI}}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>MI</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mathrm{MI}}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T})-\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{T})-\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">The assumption <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{S}}\mid\mathcal{T})=0</annotation></semantics></math> implies that the crossmodal relevance is much stronger than the internal one, <span id="A1.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MI}^{\mathrm{cross}}\rightarrow\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i},\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>MI</mi><mi>cross</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>MI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MI}^{\mathrm{cross}}\rightarrow\mathrm{MI}(\mathbf{v}_{i},\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math>. It is empirically justified under high pruning rates (less than 50% retained), where sparse selection leads to trivial intra-modal overlap.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For practical implementation, we allow balancing the crossmodal term and the intra-model term with a factor <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. As shown in Eqn. (<a href="#S3.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ 3.2 MI-Pruner ‣ 3 Methods ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), we derive two scoring functions respectively and combine them with <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Maximal Aggregation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our max aggregation over <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{select}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>select</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{select}}</annotation></semantics></math> is motivated by the LogSumExp (LSE) operator, defined as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{LSE}(z_{1},\dots,z_{N}):=\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{N}\exp(z_{j})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{LSE}(z_{1},\dots,z_{N}):=\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{N}\exp(z_{j})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As a smooth upper approximation to the maximum, the LSE operator satisfies the following bounds:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{j}z_{j}\;\leq\;\mathrm{LSE}(z_{1},\dots,z_{N})\;\leq\;\max_{j}z_{j}+\log N." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{j}z_{j}\;\leq\;\mathrm{LSE}(z_{1},\dots,z_{N})\;\leq\;\max_{j}z_{j}+\log N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we justify the maximal aggregation as a robust proxy for the overall crossmodal relevance. For simplification, we omit <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>⋅</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i},\mathbf{t}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i},\mathbf{t}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> Theoretically, let <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{j}=\text{PMI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathbf{t}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>PMI</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{j}=\text{PMI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathbf{t}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> be the log-likelihood ratio for each token pair:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{z}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{z}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The relationship between the peak signal and the total likelihood ratio can be characterized by the LSE operator:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{LSE}(\mathbf{z}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{LSE}(\mathbf{z}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\exp(\log\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\exp(\log\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Substitute Eqn. (<a href="#A1.E45" title="Equation 45 ‣ A.3 Maximal Aggregation ‣ Appendix A Theory ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) into Eqn. (<a href="#A1.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ A.3 Maximal Aggregation ‣ Appendix A Theory ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>), we obtain the lower bound of LSE, and exponentiate both sides:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{j}(\log\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{j}(\log\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{j}(\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{j}(\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\frac{p(\mathbf{t}_{j}\mid\mathbf{v}_{i})}{p(\mathbf{t}_{j})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">It’s also expressed as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{j}\left(\mathrm{PMI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathbf{t}_{j})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{j}\left(\mathrm{PMI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathbf{t}_{j})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\mathrm{PMI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathbf{t}_{j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>PMI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐭</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{N_{T}}\mathrm{PMI}(\mathbf{v}_{i};\mathbf{t}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Maximal aggregation serves as a tight lower bound for the sum of PMI, which has the same optimization direction as the global aggregation (Eqn. (<a href="#S3.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ 3.2 MI-Pruner ‣ 3 Methods ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)).
In practice, crossmodal correspondence exhibits inherent sparsity: within a sentence, typically only a few core tokens are semantically grounded in a specific visual region. Therefore, averaging these sparse, high-intensity signals with numerous irrelevant tokens leads to a noisy dilution of the relevance signal. In contrast, the max aggregation, analogous to an <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>-type norm of the association scores, captures the most salient semantic tokens and preserves the alignment measure from noise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Marginal Distribution</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="72.61" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 72.61" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,72.61) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#0000B3;" fill="#0000B3" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.98 L 0 63.63 C 0 68.59 4.02 72.61 8.98 72.61 L 468.4 72.61 C 473.36 72.61 477.38 68.59 477.38 63.63 L 477.38 8.98 C 477.38 4.02 473.36 0 468.4 0 L 8.98 0 C 4.02 0 0 4.02 0 8.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7F7FF;" fill="#F7F7FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 8.98 L 1.11 63.63 C 1.11 67.98 4.63 71.51 8.98 71.51 L 468.4 71.51 C 472.74 71.51 476.27 67.98 476.27 63.63 L 476.27 8.98 C 476.27 4.63 472.74 1.11 468.4 1.11 L 8.98 1.11 C 4.63 1.11 1.11 4.63 1.11 8.98 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.79 16.88)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.5em;--ltx-fo-height:3.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="46.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 42.82)" width="435.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.5em;">
<span id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Assumption:<span id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Each image patch occurs with equal probability <math id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})=\frac{1}{N_{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})=\frac{1}{N_{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This assumption helps to derive the marginal text probability <math id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐭</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.SS4.p1.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we recap the Law of Total Probability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jaynes, 1957</a>)</cite> and then derive <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> in Eqn. (<a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 MI-Pruner ‣ 3 Methods ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Law of Total Probability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jaynes, 1957</a>)</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be an event and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of mutually exclusive and exhaustive events.
The Law of Total Probability indicates:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(A)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}p(A\mid B_{i})\,p(B_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(A)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}p(A\mid B_{i})\,p(B_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since the mapping between a patch and a token is deterministic, <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}\}_{i=0}^{N_{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}\}_{i=0}^{N_{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> are exclusive and exhaustive. We derive the marginal probability by substituting <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j},\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j},\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{V}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})\,p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{V}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})\,p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Assuming that <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> patches are equally probable, <span id="A1.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, the prior probability <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})=\frac{1}{N_{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})=\frac{1}{N_{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Eqn. (<a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 MI-Pruner ‣ 3 Methods ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) is formulated as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{V}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})\underbrace{\frac{1}{N_{V}}}_{p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{V}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{t}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})\underbrace{\frac{1}{N_{V}}}_{p(\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">According to the Principle of Maximum Entropy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray, 2011</a>)</cite>, our uniformity is the most unbiased assumption, ensuring that the selection process is driven solely by the observed mutual information rather than predefined spatial heuristics.
It is non-trivial to obtain the appropriate prior for vision tokens. We admit potential solutions of constructing an estimator from the validation set, or linking with the patch position based on photography composition techniques (<span id="A1.SS4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, Rule of Thirds and Golden Ratio). The estimation of the prior probability is set as our future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>More Experiments</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>POPE Results</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tab. <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2 MI-Pruner ‣ 3 Methods ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
and <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Settings. ‣ 4.1 Experiments Setup ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> show the average results of POPE. In the appendix, we report detailed performance under random/popular/adversarial settings, see Tab. <a href="#A2.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ B.5 Generalization ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and <a href="#A2.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ B.5 Generalization ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. The latest Qwen3VL outperforms LLaVA1.5 across three settings, while both fall short of adversarial settings. The results after pruning hold the same tendency. Nevertheless, our method demonstrates remarkable resilience in adversarial settings, outperforming the baselines by a significant margin under different budgets. This success highlights our approach’s acute sensitivity in capturing essential visual features regarding the prompt.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>MinMax Normalizarion</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on Boltzmann distributions, we compute similarity matrices and apply softmax in Eqn. (<a href="#S3.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ 3.2 MI-Pruner ‣ 3 Methods ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>). In the appendix, we conduct an ablation study to investigate the impact of linear normalization. Specifically, we implement a two-stage MinMax normalization as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}=\operatorname{MinMax}_{j}(\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})=\frac{\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}-\operatorname{Min}_{j}(\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})}{\operatorname{Max}_{j}(\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})-\operatorname{Min}_{j}(\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>MinMax</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Min</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Min</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝆</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}=\operatorname{MinMax}_{j}(\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})=\frac{\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}-\operatorname{Min}_{j}(\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})}{\operatorname{Max}_{j}(\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})-\operatorname{Min}_{j}(\bm{\rho}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})=\operatorname{Normalize}_{j}(\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})=\frac{\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{N}\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Normalize</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{j}\mid\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{i})=\operatorname{Normalize}_{j}(\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}})=\frac{\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{N}\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\rho}}_{ij}^{\mathrm{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> first maps the raw similarity scores to the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> range, then Eqn. (<a href="#A2.E53" title="Equation 53 ‣ B.2 MinMax Normalizarion ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>) ensures a valid probability distribution across the dimension <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.
As illustrated in Tab. <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ B.2 MinMax Normalizarion ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ MI-Pruner: Crossmodal Mutual Information-guided Token Pruner for Efficient MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, our softmax normalization outperforms MinMax and maintains its overall robust performance. We attribute this performance gap to the non-linear saliency of softmax and its robustness to outliers.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A2.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study on Normalization (LLaVA1.5-7B).</span></figcaption>
